 sync_more="In sync, the rate is <b>DAW tempo ÷ division</b> (at 120 BPM: 1/4 = 2 Hz, 1/8 = 4 Hz, 1/2 = 1 Hz). While Reaper is playing, the sweep is also <b>locked to the grid</b>: each cycle starts on the beat, so the swoosh lands in the same place at every bar. When the transport is stopped, the rate still follows the project tempo. The ring is full on each division and dims in between. The state is saved with the project and in presets, and is also available in right-click › Options › Tempo sync and from MIDI (section 6).",
 s5="5. Footswitch, lights and stereo",
